
====================================================================================================
  S1  CONVENTIONS AND THE EXACT dS WORLDLINE KERNEL
====================================================================================================
  W_BD(tau) = -H^2 / (16 pi^2 sinh^2(H(tau - i eps)/2))       [Bunch & Davies 1978]
  flat limit H -> 0 gives -1/(4 pi^2 tau^2); at H > 0 it is the 4D thermal Wightman
  function at T = H/2pi exactly (Gibbons & Hawking 1977).
  S_BD(omega) = (omega/2pi)/(1 - e^{-beta omega}),  beta = 2 pi / H.

  Numerical Fourier transform of the finite-eps kernel vs e^{-omega eps} * closed form:
    omega             numeric FT         e^-we * closed     rel dev
    -1.50       3.25703166594e-5       3.25703166594e-5   1.874e-30
    -0.40       0.00645455017181       0.00645455017181   9.861e-32
     0.70        0.0882857419681        0.0882857419681         0.0
     1.00         0.112364426949         0.112364426949   9.861e-32
     2.50         0.165864152544         0.165864152544   1.972e-31
  [OK] S1a the closed-form worldline power spectrum S_BD = (w/2pi)/(1-e^-bw) reproduces the direct Fourier transform of the exact BD kernel at 5 frequencies, max rel dev 1.87e-30. This fails if the 16 pi^2 prefactor, the beta = 2pi/H identification or the i-eps sign is wrong (a 4 pi^2 prefactor would show a factor-4 miss).
  [OK] S1b A1 reconfirmed inside this parametrisation: rho_phi = omega/2pi for the thermal, the squeezed AND the illegal state (max rel dev 0.0) -- the ELEMENTARY field cannot move. Fails if the parametrisation S = c w theta(w) + n(|w|) did not enforce the c-number commutator.

====================================================================================================
  S2  CONTROL FIRST -- Bunch-Davies must give rho_O >= 0, and it does, as a theorem
====================================================================================================
  Bochner 1933: <O(tau)O(0)> is a positive-definite function of tau, so its transform
  S_O(omega) >= 0 for ANY operator in ANY state.  In a KMS state S_O(-w) = e^{-bw} S_O(w),
  hence rho_O(w) = S_O(w)(1 - e^{-bw}) >= 0 for w > 0 -- for EVERY composite, no computation.
  Explicit closed form for O = :phi^2: (one-loop bubble):
      rho_{phi^2}^{BD}(omega) = omega (omega^2 + H^2) / (24 pi^3)
  Note omega^2 + H^2: the Deser-Levin five-acceleration combination (and the standard
  thermal-bubble result) -- consistency, not evidence.

    omega           quadrature          closed form     rel dev  KMS ratio dev
     0.50    0.000839883709198    0.000839883709198         0.0            0.0
     1.00     0.00268762786943     0.00268762786943   2.958e-31      1.522e-28
     2.00      0.0134381393472      0.0134381393472   1.972e-31            0.0
     3.00      0.0403144180415      0.0403144180415   1.972e-31            0.0
  [OK] S2a CONTROL PASSES: rho_{phi^2} in Bunch-Davies equals omega(omega^2+H^2)/(24 pi^3) to 2.96e-31 at 4 frequencies, and is POSITIVE at all of them. A negative control would have been a bug; this check fails for any other coefficient than 1/(24 pi^3).
  [OK] S2b the composite power spectrum satisfies KMS at the SAME beta = 2pi/H as the elementary field (S_O(w)/S_O(-w) = e^{beta w} to 1.52e-28), which is why the control is positive by theorem and not by luck. Fails if the convolution used a non-KMS S.

====================================================================================================
  S3  THE THEOREM -- every stationary Gaussian state, and rho_O moves ONE WAY only
====================================================================================================
  Split S = V + N with V(nu) = c nu theta(nu) (vacuum) and N(nu) = n(|nu|) (EVEN, >= 0).
  S*S = V*V + 2 V*N + N*N.  N*N is even in omega, so it drops out of rho_O = S_O(w)-S_O(-w).
      V*V   : antisymmetric part = c^2 omega^3/6           -> omega^3/(24 pi^3)
      2 V*N : antisymmetric part = 2c * 2 omega * N        -> (2/pi^2) N omega
  because Int_0^inf nu n(|w-nu|) dnu - Int_0^inf nu n(w+nu) dnu = 2 w Int_0^inf n  exactly.
  =>   rho_{phi^2}(omega) = omega^3/(24 pi^3) + (2/pi^2) N omega,   N = Int_0^inf n >= 0.
  The state enters through ONE non-negative number.  Verified against quadrature, which knows
  nothing about the derivation:

  state                               N  omega         quadrature            theorem    rel dev
  BD (thermal)              0.006631456   0.70     0.001401597934     0.001401597934        0.0
  BD (thermal)              0.006631456   2.00      0.01343813935      0.01343813935  1.972e-31
  squeezed r=1 @ w=1         0.20147934   0.70      0.02904069842      0.02904070352   1.755e-7
  squeezed r=1 @ w=1         0.20147934   2.00      0.09240701093      0.09240701244   1.634e-8
  squeezed r=2 @ w=3          11.138761   0.70        1.580490339        1.580490339  1.665e-11
  squeezed r=2 @ w=3          11.138761   2.00        4.525120238        4.525120257   4.054e-9
  squeezed r=0.4 @ w=0.3    0.010239773   0.70      0.00191343627     0.001913436494   1.174e-7
  squeezed r=0.4 @ w=0.3    0.010239773   2.00      0.01490053523      0.01490053523  2.204e-11
  NOT A STATE: n<0         -0.037576252   0.70    -0.004869253151    -0.004869250274    5.91e-7
  NOT A STATE: n<0         -0.037576252   2.00     -0.00447857013    -0.004478569817   6.994e-8
  [OK] S3a the theorem rho = w^3/(24 pi^3) + (2/pi^2) N w reproduces independent 30-digit quadrature for 5 states (thermal, three squeezings, and one ILLEGAL negative-occupation state) at 2 frequencies each, max rel dev 5.91e-7. Fails if the antisymmetric part of 2 V*N were anything other than 4 c omega N -- e.g. a missing factor 2 shows up as 100%.
  [OK] S3b NO NEGATIVE BAND in any admissible state: the smallest rho_{phi^2} over the four legal states is 0.0014016 > 0. Fails the moment any legal state produces rho < 0.
  [OK] S3c the check above has teeth: relaxing state positivity (n < 0 in a band, which is NOT a density matrix) DOES drive rho_{phi^2} negative. So S3b is a statement about positivity of the state, not an artefact of the estimator.

