====================================================================================================
  S4  HOW DEEP A NEGATIVE BAND WOULD NEED TO BE -- it needs a NEGATIVE total occupation
====================================================================================================
  rho_{phi^2}(w) < 0  <=>  N < -w^2/(48 pi).  Compare with Bunch-Davies N = H^2/(48 pi):
   omega/H         N required               N_BD      ratio
      0.50    -0.001657863991     0.006631455962      -0.25
      1.00    -0.006631455962     0.006631455962       -1.0
      2.00     -0.02652582385     0.006631455962       -4.0
  [OK] S4a the analytic Bunch-Davies occupation weight N = H^2/(48 pi) = 0.006631455962 matches the quadrature 0.006631455962. Fails for any other zeta(2) bookkeeping.
  [OK] S4b at omega = H the required occupation weight is EXACTLY minus the Bunch-Davies value (ratio -1.0), and it is negative at every omega. A negative band is not a small correction to a state: it is a state with negative total particle content. Fails if the required N were merely small-and-positive.

====================================================================================================
  S5  DERIVATIVE-COUPLED COMPOSITE, AND WHERE A NEGATIVE BAND *WOULD* HAVE TO LIVE
====================================================================================================
  For O = :(d_tau phi)^2: each propagator carries d d', so the Wick weight is (nu nu')^2:
      rho(w) = [ c^2 w^7/140 + 2c ( w^3 M2 + 3 w M4 ) ] / pi,   M_n = Int nu^n N(nu) dnu >= 0
  -> positive again, by the same parity argument (odd powers of nu die against even N).

  state                   omega         quadrature        closed form    rel dev
  BD (thermal)             0.50    0.0001132343215    0.0001132343215        0.0
  BD (thermal)             1.50     0.001725511085     0.001725511085        0.0
  BD (thermal)             3.00       0.1301579782       0.1301579782        0.0
  squeezed r=1 @ w=1       0.50       0.1540033973       0.1540033973  8.522e-14
  squeezed r=1 @ w=1       1.50       0.6262310591       0.6262310591  6.258e-12
  squeezed r=1 @ w=1       3.00        2.478305722        2.478305722  7.221e-18
  [OK] S5a the derivative-coupled composite :(d_tau phi)^2: matches its closed form to 6.26e-12 and is POSITIVE at every point tested (min 0.000113234). So the escape is not restored by putting derivatives in the coupling. Fails if the omega^7/140 Beta-function coefficient or either moment weight were wrong.

  The ODD weight nu(w-nu) DOES give a negative band -- and it is NOT an operator:
  weight                  S_O(-0.5)           S_O(0)        S_O(+0.5)   Bochner S_O>=0?
  (nu nu')^0          0.00011917299    0.00067190697     0.0027577455               YES
  (nu nu')^1          -1.7875948e-5   -0.00013438139   -0.00041366182 NO -- not an operator
  (nu nu')^2           1.6067072e-5      9.598671e-5    0.00037180319               YES
  [OK] S5b the odd weight produces a genuine negative band (rho = -0.000125983 at w = 0.5) but violates Bochner positivity (S_O(0) = -0.000413662 < 0), so it is the power spectrum of NO operator, while the two even weights pass. This pins the escape precisely: it requires a Bochner-admissible weight that is not an even polynomial in each argument. Fails if any even weight went negative or the odd one did not.

====================================================================================================
  S6  DOOR A4 -- the squeezing de Sitter actually realises, as a number
====================================================================================================
  Super-horizon dS squeezing grows as r_sq ~ N_efolds (standard inflationary result); a mode
  squeezed by r_sq carries sinh^2(r_sq) quanta, so N grows like sinh^2(r_sq) -- and rho_O grows
  with it, in the ANTI-MOND direction.
   N_efolds     sinh^2(r_sq)    rho_O/rho_O^BD at w=H
          1     1.381098e+00                15.691184
          5     5.506116e+03                58571.341
         10     1.212913e+08             1.2902148e+9
         60     3.260452e+51            3.4682484e+52
  [OK] S6a at the e-fold counts dS actually realises the squeezed occupation makes rho_O larger by 3.468e+52 -- ~52 orders of magnitude, and in the WRONG direction. Door A4 closes with a number: realised squeezing is not near a sign flip, it is the opposite of near. Fails if the amplification were O(1) or negative.

====================================================================================================
  S7  PHYSICAL NUMBERS, BOTH FOOTINGS, AND THE INERTIA LAW (R5, R6)
====================================================================================================
  R6 bookkeeping: the object computed here is a spectral density, but every acceleration below
  is a_0, not the floor.  a_0 canonical 9.3614e-11  floor k = 4.6807e-11
                          a_0 ALT       1.1300e-10  floor k = 5.6500e-11
  Each footing is rebuilt from its OWN cH (canonical cH_Lambda, ALT cH_0 = 1.2082 cH_Lambda) so
  that the two are related by exactly one factor, not by the rounding of the quoted a_0:
    canonical  cH = 5.41943e-10  ->  a_0 = cH/Z = 9.36190e-11  (locked 9.36140e-11, dev 5.35e-05)
    ALT        cH = 6.54775e-10  ->  a_0 = cH/Z = 1.13110e-10  (locked 1.13000e-10, dev 9.78e-04)
  [OK] S7a0 both footings reproduce their locked a_0 from cH/Z to 9.78e-04 (canonical 9.3614e-11, ALT 1.13e-10). Fails if Z, the 1.2082 = 1/sqrt(Omega_L), or the cH_Lambda-vs-cH_0 assignment were wrong -- using 2Z instead of Z misses by a factor 2.

  footing        H_dS [1/s]   w=a_0/c [1/s]     rho_O(a_0/c)   N required (<0)
  canonical     1.80773e-18     3.12279e-19      1.41227e-57      -6.46689e-40
  ALT           2.18409e-18     3.77296e-19      2.49078e-57      -9.44003e-40
  rho_O scales as w(w^2+H^2) and both w and H carry one factor 1.2082, so the predicted
  ratio is 1.763666615; got 1.763666615 (rel dev 1.94e-17; the inputs are float64, hence ~1e-16)
  [OK] S7a the verdict is footing-independent: rho_O > 0 on BOTH footings, and the ALT/canonical ratio is exactly the cube of the footing factor (1.763667). Fails if a footing were mixed -- canonical H with ALT omega gives 1.208, not 1.764.

  delta_m ~ (2/pi) P Int rho_O(w)/w^2 dw over the committed window w_c in [1.78e-14, 2.21e-14]
  (the free fifth constant), IR-regulated at w = H_dS:
    canonical  delta_m coefficient in [1.3552810004e-31, 2.08917041288e-31]  (units of the coupling^2; only the SIGN is claimed)
    ALT        delta_m coefficient in [1.35528110444e-31, 2.0891705197e-31]  (units of the coupling^2; only the SIGN is claimed)
    the two footings agree to ~1e-7 because the integral is dominated by w_c^2/2 and the footing
    enters only through the H^2 ln(w_c/H) piece -- delta_m here is essentially footing-blind,
    which is a statement about this estimator, not evidence for either footing.
  [OK] S7b delta_m > 0 across the whole committed omega_c window on both footings -- inertia is INCREASED, i.e. anti-MOND. Fails if any admissible omega_c or footing flipped the sign; the integrand is rho_O/w^2 > 0 pointwise, so the only way to flip it is a negative band.

  Feed the framework's own temperature in (Deser & Levin 1997; Narnhofer, Peter & Thirring
  1996): 2 pi T = sqrt(a^2/c^2 + H^2), i.e. H^2 -> H^2 + a^2/c^2, hence
      delta_m(a) - delta_m(0) = (2/pi) (a^2/c^2) ln(w_c/H) / (24 pi^3)  >  0,
  so m(a) = m0 (1 + K a^2) with K > 0: inertia GROWS with acceleration and mu -> 1 as a -> 0.
  The framework's own kernel nu(y) = sqrt(1+1/y) (Milgrom 1999 PLA 253:273 eqs 6-9) needs
  modified inertia m_eff/m = 1/nu(y), i.e. delta_m/m = 1/nu - 1 < 0 for ALL y, -> -1 in deep MOND.
    canonical  y = g_bar/a_0 = 0.10682 at g_bar = 1e-11 m/s^2  ->  required delta_m/m = -0.6893;  computed K = 8.75234e-20 (> 0)
    ALT        y = g_bar/a_0 = 0.08850 at g_bar = 1e-11 m/s^2  ->  required delta_m/m = -0.7149;  computed K = 8.57231e-20 (> 0)
  [OK] S7c NO MOND LIMIT in this class: the required fractional mass shift is -0.6893 (canonical) / -0.7149 (ALT) at g_bar = 1e-11, while the class delivers a POSITIVE, a^2-growing shift (K > 0 on both footings). Fails if K came out negative, or if the framework's own kernel wanted delta_m > 0.

====================================================================================================
  S8  DOOR A5 -- is a negative band a physical density matrix at all?
====================================================================================================
  (i) SECULAR (Davies/Lindblad) generator. For linear coupling to a bath operator O with
      power spectrum S_O, the Kossakowski matrix in the {a, a^dag} basis is
          K = diag( S_O(+w_0), S_O(-w_0) ),
      and complete positivity requires both entries >= 0 (Gorini-Kossakowski-Sudarshan 1976,
      Lindblad 1976). Since S_O(w) = rho_O(w)/(1 - e^{-beta w}) and the denominator is positive
      for w > 0, a negative band at the system frequency gives a NEGATIVE RATE at ANY depth.

    band depth d       rho(w_b=2)       Gamma_down    CP?
    0.000000e+00      0.013438139      0.013438186    yes
    6.719070e-03     0.0067190697     0.0067190931    yes
    1.342470e-02     1.3438139e-5     1.3438186e-5    yes
    1.345158e-02    -1.3438139e-5    -1.3438186e-5     NO
    2.687628e-02     -0.013438139     -0.013438186     NO
  [OK] S8a the CP boundary in the secular generator sits EXACTLY where rho crosses zero: at 0.999x the zero-crossing depth the rate is +1.344e-05 and at 1.001x it is -1.344e-05. So the CP cap on band depth is 'no negative band at all', not some finite tolerance. Fails if a negative rho gave a non-negative rate.

  (ii) TWO CAPS, side by side (the corpus's own bound vs this one).
       ghost / mu_eff cap:  mu_eff = 1 + rho/2 > 0  =>  rho > -2   (tn18 sits at 80% of it)
       complete positivity: rho >= 0 everywhere    =>  ZERO negative band admitted
       => CP is strictly the tighter of the two; a band at 80% of the ghost cap has rho ~ -1.6,
          which is not a completely positive dynamical map. A MOND state that is not a density
          matrix is not a result.
  [OK] S8b the corpus's tn18 band (80% of the ghost cap, rho_min = -1.6) is INSIDE the ghost cap rho > -2 but OUTSIDE the CP cap rho >= 0, so the two caps genuinely disagree about it and CP is the binding one. Fails if tn18's depth were either ghost-excluded or CP-allowed.

  (iii) NON-SECULAR Caldeira-Leggett form, with the Dekker inequality
        K = [[D_pp, -D_xp - i lam/2], [-D_xp + i lam/2, D_xx]],  CP <=> D_pp D_xx - D_xp^2 >= lam^2/4
        (Dekker 1977; Sandulescu & Scutaru 1987).  MODEL, labelled: flat form factor up to w_c,
        IR regulator at w = H, D_xp = 0, lam = (pi/2) rho'(0).
        control, positive bath: D_pp = 0.11288149  D_xx = 0.0091450898  lam = 0.002110858
          D_pp D_xx = 0.0010323114   vs  lam^2/4 = 1.1139304e-6   -> min eig = 0.0091343529
          but the TRUNCATED CL generator (D_xx set to 0) gives det = -1.1139304e-6 < 0 even for this perfectly POSITIVE bath
  [OK] S8c control: the full CL Kossakowski matrix is positive for a positive bath (min eigenvalue 0.00913435), while the usual D_xx = 0 truncation violates Dekker even then. So 'the CL equation is not CP' is an artefact of the truncation and is NOT evidence about a negative band -- worth stating because door D4 could otherwise read it as one. Fails if the full matrix were also non-positive.

   band width  depth d* where min eig -> 0   d*/(pointwise rho=0 depth)
         0.25                 0.1609155666                        11.97
         0.50                0.07487212142                         5.57
         1.00                0.03820370543                         2.84
  [OK] S8d in the integrated CL form the CP boundary depth DECREASES monotonically with band width (0.160916 -> 0.0382037 for widths 0.25 -> 1.0) and every one of them is deeper than the pointwise rho = 0 depth by 6-25x -- so the broadband test is the PERMISSIVE one and the secular test in S8a is the binding one. Fails if a wider band needed a deeper depth, which would mean the integral was not doing the work.

====================================================================================================
  S9  PROVE BY MOVING THE NUMBER, AND REFINE
====================================================================================================
  H = 1.0:  N = 0.006631455962   rho_O(1.3) = 0.00469931733   H^2-part = 0.001746958115
  H = 2.0:  N = 0.02652582385   rho_O(1.3) = 0.009940191675   H^2-part = 0.006987832461
  [OK] S9a SHOULD move: doubling H multiplies the H^2 part of rho_O by exactly 4.0 (predicted 4), while the omega^3 part is H-independent. Fails for any other H-scaling, e.g. if N had picked up a stray beta.
  same rho_O(1.1) with different quadrature split points: 0.0032668116752962 vs 0.0032668116752962
  [OK] S9b SHOULD NOT move: changing the quadrature split points (40,5) -> (80,2) leaves rho_O fixed to 0.0. Fails if the integrand's exponential tail or its two kinks were being mis-sampled.
  refinement dps 30 -> 40: rho_O(1.1) shifts by 5.132e-32 (closed form 0.0032668116752962)
  [OK] S9c refining the working precision from 30 to 40 digits moves rho_O by 5.13e-32, far below the 1e-6 the sign conclusions need, so nothing here is a precision artefact. Fails if the quadrature had been resolving a cancellation only accidentally.

====================================================================================================
  S10  FREE PARAMETER COUNT (R1)
====================================================================================================
  free dimensionless parameters before: 1   after: 1
  Had the escape worked it would have ADDED one (the squeezing r_sq, or equivalently N), so the
  best case for this door was a REPARAMETRISATION, not a derivation. And rho_O depends on the
  state through exactly ONE number N (S3d), which is bounded below by zero -- there is no knob
  in this class that can be turned toward MOND at all.
  [OK] S10a the free-parameter count is unchanged at 1 (kappa), and the single state parameter this door could have introduced, N, is positive for every state examined (N_BD = 0.00663146). Nothing here derives kappa. Fails if any state had given N <= 0, which is the only way this door could have supplied a mechanism.

====================================================================================================
  RESULT
====================================================================================================
  25/25 checks held.
  LANE C VERDICT. The composite operator does exactly what door A3 predicted -- it makes rho
  genuinely state-dependent, unlike the elementary field -- and the dependence is ONE-SIGNED:
      rho_{phi^2}(omega) = omega^3/(24 pi^3) + (2/pi^2) N omega,   N = Int_0^inf S(-nu) dnu >= 0,
  for every stationary Gaussian state, with Bunch-Davies the minimum (N = H^2/48pi, giving the closed
  form omega(omega^2+H^2)/(24 pi^3)).  Squeezing -- alpha-vacua included -- only raises N, so it
  DEEPENS the anti-MOND wall; at realised e-fold counts by ~52 orders of magnitude.  A negative band
  needs N < -omega^2/(48 pi), i.e. negative total occupation, which is not a density matrix; and if one
  posits such a band anyway it makes a secular Lindblad rate negative at ANY depth, so it is not
  completely positive either.  delta_m > 0 on both footings across the whole committed omega_c window,
  and feeding in the Deser-Levin temperature gives m(a) = m0(1 + K a^2) with K > 0 -- inertia grows
  with acceleration, while the framework's own kernel needs delta_m/m = 1/nu - 1 ~ -0.70 at
  g_bar = 1e-11.  AGAINST INTEREST: this closes the escape the corpus was counting on, and the pretty
  omega^2+H^2 five-acceleration structure appears and still gives the wrong sign.
  SCOPE: stationary Gaussian states, quadratic composites with even Wick weights. Outside it, and NOT
  excluded here: non-Gaussian states, genuinely non-stationary squeezing, bounded/finite-level sectors
  (door A2), and mixed composites such as T_mu_nu whose Wick weight need not be a positive-coefficient
  polynomial -- S5b shows exactly what such a weight would have to look like, and that it must still
  pass Bochner.  No closure is claimed.
  kappa = 1/2 remains FITTED, NOT DERIVED.
